// The story's chapter scenes, played when a chapter begins (ChapterDef.inkScene names the knot).

=== chapter_1 ===
The key is heavier than you expected.
The shop smells of lavender and old wool. Dust hangs in the last of the sunlight. On the counter, your great-aunt's pattern book waits, a few pages torn out.
A note is tucked inside the cover, in looping handwriting.
"For whoever comes next. The shop opens at dusk. The town will tell you what it needs; you only have to listen. Love, Aunt Win."
* [Turn the sign to OPEN]
- The bell over the door rings for the first time in a long time.
-> END

=== chapter_2 ===
Juno lingers by the yarn baskets.
Juno: You knit, right? Everyone says your great-aunt could knit anything.
Under the counter you find her needles, a half-finished row still on them. You pick up where she left off.
Knitting is open!
-> END

=== chapter_3 ===
Old Tobias puts a photograph on the counter: a tablecloth with the sea embroidered round its edge.
Tobias: Elsa made it. I'd know it anywhere.
Your great-aunt's book has an embroidery section, and a page torn out of it.
Embroidery is open!
-> END

=== chapter_4 ===
A new shop opens across the square: Knot & Needle, all crisp paper bags and crochet in the window.
Its owner leans in your doorway.
Rowan: Healthy competition. Welcome to the neighbourhood, I suppose.
They leave a crochet hook on your counter, and a business card with a heart drawn on the back. Then they cross it out.
Crochet is open!
-> END

=== chapter_5 ===
The festival committee knocks at closing time.
This year's Community Quilt needs a patch from each of your friends, and someone has to sew it all together.
That someone is you.
The old sewing machine in the corner hums when you plug it in, as if it remembers.
Sewing is open!
-> END
